`normalizeGatewayUri` (`gateway_client.dart:141-165`) maps `http://`→`ws://` and `https://`→`wss://`, and prepends `ws://` to a scheme-less string. The socket layer is a plain `dart:io` connect with no certificate pinning (`lib/data/datasources/remote/gateway/gateway_socket.dart:71-74`).

## 4. Authority granted to the destination

On authentication success the client advertises the device's tool manifest (`gateway_client.dart:240-249` → `_sendToolManifest` at `:299-307`), the chat screen starts the RPC listener (`lib/presentation/screen/chat/chat_screen.dart:236-243` → `lib/presentation/screen/gateway/cubit/gateway_rpc_cubit.dart:117-124`), and incoming frames are dispatched to the tool registry (`lib/domain/services/gateway/gateway_rpc_receiver.dart:148`). The Tier-2 permission check is advisory and self-granting for the highest-value tools: `read_device_file` is registered with `checkPermission: () => service.checkPermission()` (`lib/domain/tools/chat/tool_registry.dart:782`) which resolves to a hardcoded `true` (`lib/data/datasources/tools/chat/file_workspace_service.dart:78`), and its read path applies no path containment (`file_workspace_service.dart:149-175`); `read_recent_notifications` (`tool_registry.dart:841`) and `extract_latest_otp` (`:871`) call `NotificationTriageService.checkPermission` which grants the permission itself (`lib/data/datasources/tools/chat/notification_triage_service.dart:201-212`); `clipboard_read` is Tier-1 auto-executing (`tool_registry.dart:267,273`).

## 5. User-visible confirmation

Pairing ends with a success snackbar whose text is the attacker-supplied profile name:

```dart title=lib/presentation/screen/chat/chat_screen.dart startLineNumber=1226 endLineNumber=1237
